/**
 * Planning-scoped log of the learned-state reads one planning makes, and their replay.
 *
 * <p>
 * A planning that is reproducible is a deterministic function of its query, the data and statistics it read and the
 * learned state it read. Each learned read is recorded here by the owner of that state (the operator feedback, the
 * filter selectivity statistics and the learned filter selectivity), not by its callers, so no reader can bypass it:
 * the read's kind, the key references and inputs its outcome depends on, and the outcome as the planner consumes it.
 * State that has no side-effect-free re-read is guarded instead by its owner's version of exactly that state. A
 * {@link Log#replay replay} re-executes every recorded read against the current state without side effects and says
 * whether each still answers the same (exactly, or within a tolerance).
 *
 * <p>
 * The log is thread-local and opened beside {@link LmdbPlanningWallClockCuts}: inner scopes join the outermost, which
 * every publisher of a plan already brackets. Outside a scope, and while a replay re-reads, recording is a no-op. The
 * recorder is reused by its thread, so a read allocates nothing beyond the growth of the grouped encoding: the reads of
 * one key (the dimensions of one physical cell) share one key group, and only a read that returned an estimate stores
 * its predicted input and its values.
 */
